            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-catalina/plat-svc/files/clemente/standby-power-enable",
                    "line": 230,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I'd like this to be re-written in a way to rely less on low-level i2c operations but reuse existing daemons.  There is an LED manager for setting LEDs, there is nvme sensor for finding if we can talk to the nvme drive, etc."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-catalina/plat-svc/files/clemente/standby-power-enable",
                    "line": 230,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alex-TS-Wang",
                        "email": "alex.ts.wang@fii-foxconn.com",
                        "username": "Alex-TS-Wang"
                    },
                    "message": "I\u2019ve updated the implementation to rely on existing daemons instead of low-level I2C operations:\n\nThe presence of the boot drive is now determined via the BOOTDRIVE_TEMP_C NVMe sensor\u2019s Available property.\n\nLED control is handled through the phosphor-ledcontroller service, using the \"hdd_led\" identifier.\n\nThis removes direct I2C/CPLD accesses and reuses the system\u2019s existing sensor and LED management services."
                }
            ],
